<main class="cs26" id="main">
<section class="hero26" aria-labelledby="page-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="crumbs"><a href="/">CallTeam</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/case-studies/">Case studies</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Financial services</span></div><div class="hero-grid"><div><div class="kicker">Financial services appointment-setting case study</div><h1 id="page-title">18 booked meetings for specialist financial services.</h1><p class="lead">An outsourced analyst and financial research provider needed to reach busy finance decision-makers. The campaign made the offer concrete: support the deal work a team needs to complete when internal resources are stretched.</p><div class="tags"><span class="tag">B2B financial services</span><span class="tag">Outsourced analyst support</span><span class="tag">Human calling</span></div><div class="actions"><a href="#campaign-result" class="button">See the campaign result <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="button alt" href="https://calendly.com/hello-callteam/new-meeting">Book a Free 30-Minute Call <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div><aside class="ledger" aria-label="Reported campaign result"><div class="ledger-top"><span>CAMPAIGN RECORD</span><span>CLIENT CONFIDENTIAL</span></div><div class="ledger-number">18</div><div class="ledger-label">booked sales meetings</div><p>Research. Models. Deal support. A specific conversation about the work.</p><div class="ledger-footer"><div><strong>90 days</strong><span>first campaign period</span></div><div><strong>B2B</strong><span>finance and advisory buyers</span></div></div><div class="ledger-flow"><span>Relevant context</span><span>Workload question</span><span>Agreed meeting</span></div></aside></div><div class="evidence-caption">Client identity withheld.</div><nav class="jumpbar" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#company">Company and buyers</a><a href="#approach">Campaign approach</a><a href="#campaign-result">Results</a><a href="#apply">Tools and resources</a><a href="#questions">Questions</a></nav></div></section>
<section id="company" aria-labelledby="company-heading"><div class="wrap intro-grid"><div><div class="kicker">Company and market</div><h2 id="company-heading">An expert services offer, made specific enough to discuss.</h2><p>The company provided financial research and analyst support, including models, comparable-company analysis, pitch materials and deal-execution work. It helped investment banks, advisory teams and other relevant finance buyers explore outside support for defined work.</p><p>The outreach needed to establish where external support could fit. Event contacts provided useful context for some conversations; calling and follow-up then tested the requirement, the current model and the next step.</p></div><dl class="fact-list"><div><dt>Company type</dt><dd>Outsourced financial research and analyst-support provider</dd></div><div><dt>Target buyers</dt><dd>Relevant leaders in investment banking, advisory, private capital and finance</dd></div><div><dt>Campaign window</dt><dd>First 90 days</dd></div><div><dt>Reported result</dt><dd>18 booked meetings</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<section class="tint" aria-labelledby="problem-heading"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker">The commercial problem</div><h2 id="problem-heading">Expertise needed a concrete job to attach to.</h2><p class="section-intro">Finance buyers could keep the work inside, use an existing provider or decide there was no need to act. The caller had to discover which situation actually applied.</p><div class="three"><article class="detail-card"><span class="card-no">01</span><h3>Workload</h3><p>Was there a research or deal-execution task that an external team could usefully support?</p></article><article class="detail-card"><span class="card-no">02</span><h3>Trust</h3><p>Could the buyer understand the work on offer without a vague promise of cheaper resources?</p></article><article class="detail-card"><span class="card-no">03</span><h3>Timing</h3><p>Was there a reason for a conversation now, or a clear condition for coming back later?</p></article></div></div></section>
<section id="approach" aria-labelledby="message-heading"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker">The conversation strategy</div><h2 id="message-heading">Give the buyer a specific question to answer.</h2><div class="message-grid"><div class="message-old"><span class="label">The broad pitch to avoid</span><p>A general introduction to an experienced outsourcing team.</p></div><div class="message-new"><span class="label">The campaign’s practical direction</span><blockquote>When deal work picks up, how are you handling the extra models, research and pitch preparation?</blockquote></div></div><p class="caption">Adapted from the campaign’s analyst-support talk track. It gives the buyer room to explain that the work is covered, worth exploring or relevant later.</p><div style="margin-top:48px"><div class="kicker">Execution decisions</div><h2>Use the context. Qualify the work. Earn the next step.</h2><ol class="steps"><li><h3>Select a relevant contact</h3><p>Prioritize a plausible finance buyer and use event context only where that connection genuinely existed.</p></li><li><h3>Name the work</h3><p>Explain the research, modelling or execution support before describing broad outsourcing credentials.</p></li><li><h3>Explore the current model</h3><p>Ask how the team handles demand and listen for internal coverage, budget constraints or a specific support need.</p></li><li><h3>Coordinate the meeting</h3><p>Agree a purpose, work through timing and give the host the context needed to continue the discussion.</p></li></ol></div><aside class="handoff" aria-label="Useful sales handoff fields"><div><span class="kicker">Qualification and handoff</span><h3>Keep the buyer’s reason in the handoff.</h3><p>The useful detail is the work the prospect wants to discuss, together with any constraint the host needs to know.</p></div><dl><div><dt>Account context</dt><dd>Relevant finance or advisory role and any genuine prior connection</dd></div><div><dt>Area of interest</dt><dd>Research, modelling, pitch work or another defined service</dd></div><div><dt>Current position</dt><dd>Internal resources, budget, timing and known alternatives</dd></div><div><dt>Next step</dt><dd>Agreed meeting purpose, scheduling and follow-up owner</dd></div></dl></aside></div></section>
<section id="campaign-result" class="tint" aria-labelledby="result-heading"><div class="wrap result-grid"><div><div class="kicker">The campaign result</div><h2 id="result-heading">Eighteen booked meetings in the first 90 days.</h2><p>The first 90 days produced 18 booked meetings for the outsourced financial research and analyst-support offer.</p><p>The case shows the work behind those bookings: making an expert service understandable, exploring the buyer’s current resources and following up with a clear purpose.</p><div class="measure-note"><p>The result covers booked meetings during the stated period. Attendance and downstream sales figures were not reported.</p></div></div><aside class="result-panel" aria-label="Campaign result figures"><div class="kicker">One campaign. Its actual period.</div><div class="result-row"><strong>18</strong><span>booked meetings</span></div><div class="result-row"><strong>90</strong><span>campaign days</span></div><p class="result-note">Results cover this campaign and period. Individual campaign outcomes vary.</p></aside></div></section>
